On Saturday 15 May 2004 21:04 Digi (symet@goroboticsSPAMTRAP.net) wrote:

> After a few rounds, the Troll came back to life, picked up
> some equipment, and attacked me again.  I killed him, he 
> reanimated, this continued
> for some time until I finally ate his corpse.  What caused him to keep
> reanimating?  

Trollishness. It's what trolls do (all T, up to Olog-hai). There's a
thread about how to stop them reanimating at the moment; eating them is
one of the ways, indeed, but they can even reanimate while you're in
the course of eating them.

> Also, will eating a leprechaun corpse cause you to 
> randomly teleport?

Yes. At least, it gives you a (largish) chance of gaining the teleport
intrinsic. There's no way to get rid of this, but it can be controlled.
In controlled form it's even useful.

Nymphs have the same effect. Tengu can give you either teleportitis or
teleport control. Whether or not you already have one or the other
extrinsically doesn't affect the chance.

